{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You were admitted for vomiting again—can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been vomiting nonstop since yesterday—maybe 10 times. I just can’t keep anything down. I was only home a few days from the last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And it’s bilious—greenish? Any blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Green, yes. No blood that I’ve seen this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:09:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ve reviewed your history—Type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, gastric pacer, and you’ve had Botox in the stomach before. But your symptoms keep coming back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:10:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and the pacer didn’t help much. I thought maybe the Botox would, but it only lasted a little while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:11:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now. You’ll get fluids and medications through your port to help with nausea and hydration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:12:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Again? It’s hard not eating. But I guess it’s necessary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, just until we get the vomiting under control. We also need to adjust your insulin since you’re not eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:15:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugars have been high. I’m worried about that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your glucose was 273 when you came in—elevated, but not dangerous. We’ll give you a sliding scale and adjust your long-acting insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:17:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. My blood pressure’s been high too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was 190/100. We’ve increased your lisinopril and switched your metoprolol to the long-acting version. We may need IV meds if it stays high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on those for years. I don’t want a stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. Your labs look stable—hemoglobin is 12, so no anemia right now. White count is slightly high, but no infection signs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:22:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been so anxious lately. Is that part of this?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Anxiety can definitely play a role. We’ve consulted GI and social work. There’s some discussion about whether this is more cyclic vomiting syndrome than gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:25:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What’s the difference?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:26:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Gastroparesis is delayed stomach emptying. Cyclic vomiting is more like migraine-related episodes—sudden, severe vomiting without a structural cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:27:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t get headaches though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not everyone does. Some people have it without migraines. We’re considering switching your antidepressant to amitriptyline—it can help prevent these episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:30:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on citalopram now. Is that okay to stop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:31:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll taper it slowly—half a tablet daily for a week, then stop. Amitriptyline at bedtime may help with both mood and vomiting prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-02-10 13:32:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-02-11 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You didn’t vomit overnight—that’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-02-11 09:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I feel like I might still throw up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-02-11 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "But you haven’t. We’d like to try a small amount of clear liquids today—if you tolerate that, we can advance your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-02-11 09:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can try. Just water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-02-11 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, small sips. We’ll monitor you closely. Your blood pressure is better—145/88 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-02-11 09:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well—tolerating liquids, no vomiting. We’re going to try a soft diet today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have toast or applesauce?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. Small portions. And we’ll keep your anti-nausea meds on board."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on Reglan for years. Is that still okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re keeping it for now, but your GI doctor is concerned about long-term use—possible tardive dyskinesia. We’ll discuss alternatives at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard about that. Maybe we should stop it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor. For now, it’s helping. Also, your urine culture showed contamination—no infection, so no antibiotics needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-02-12 10:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. I was worried about a UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had two full meals and no vomiting. That’s excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel almost normal. Can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. But there’s an option to stay one more night for an EGD with possible Botox repeat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to stay. I feel fine now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. We’ll discharge you. But please call Dr. Patel’s office on Monday to schedule the EGD if you change your mind."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:36:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take amitriptyline at night, higher dose of lisinopril, and stay on Protonix. Zofran as needed, and Reglan before meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:38:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Resume your usual glargine dose at bedtime. Check sugars regularly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:41:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I need to see my psychiatrist too, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2199-02-13 09:42:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, please follow up with them about the cyclic vomiting and anxiety. And your PCP for overall management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2199-02-14 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. You’ve been asymptomatic, eating well, and your vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2199-02-14 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll call Dr. Patel and my psychiatrist this week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2199-02-14 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. If vomiting returns, come back right away. Otherwise, we’ll see how the new meds work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2199-02-14 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope this time is different."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2199-02-14 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adjusting the plan to target cyclic vomiting more directly. Amitriptyline may make a difference. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2199-02-14 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-02-10 12:58:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-02-14 12:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with Type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and a history of recurrent vomiting was readmitted for intractable vomiting, just days after a prior discharge. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, and antiemetics. Her blood pressure was elevated initially, requiring adjustment of antihypertensives, including temporary IV medications. Insulin was titrated due to fasting and hyperglycemia. The clinical team leaned toward cyclic vomiting syndrome over gastroparesis, given her recurrent episodes and lack of electrolyte imbalances despite frequent vomiting. She was transitioned from citalopram to amitriptyline for potential migraine-related vomiting prevention. She tolerated advancement to a regular diet, remained asymptomatic, and requested early discharge. She was discharged home with instructions to follow up with her GI specialist to consider repeat EGD with Botox, and with her psychiatrist and PCP for ongoing management of cyclic vomiting and mood.",
    "problems": [
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
